{"timestamp": 1779379576.929493, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I reported in Electrical \u2014 Eve\u2019s body was right there with me when I got in. Meeting also shows Alice is dead, but I didn\u2019t see her body.\n\nMy route was cafeteria \u2192 oxygen \u2192 upper engine \u2192 lower engine \u2192 storage \u2192 medbay \u2192 electrical. I saw Eve in oxygen around ticks 5-6, then again in upper engine around tick 9. I saw Diana in lower engine ticks 12-14. I saw Bob in medbay at tick 19, right before I went into electrical and found Eve.\n\nI never saw Alice this round. Bob was the last person I saw near the area before the report, but I\u2019m not hard accusing yet \u2014 just giving the info."}}
{"timestamp": 1779379593.0059469, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I started in medbay, then went upper engine \u2192 lower engine \u2192 storage \u2192 navigation. I saw Bob in medbay early, ticks 2-4, coming in from electrical. Then I saw Frank enter upper engine from oxygen around tick 6, and Eve entered upper engine from oxygen around tick 8. Eve left upper engine toward medbay at tick 9. I saw Frank again in lower engine ticks 12-14, so that part of his route checks out.\n\nI didn\u2019t see Alice at all and I didn\u2019t see any bodies. Since Eve went toward medbay/electrical side after I last saw her, and Frank says Bob was in medbay at tick 19 right before the body in electrical, Bob is the main person I\u2019d want to hear from. Not a hard accuse yet, but Bob has the most relevant placement to Eve\u2019s body from what we know."}}
{"timestamp": 1779379623.1274502, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Diana's timeline for the start is spot on \u2014 we were in Medbay together around ticks 2-4. \n\nAfter that, I went straight up to Cafeteria, headed right to Weapons for a task, and then eventually came back down to Medbay to finish my Submit Scan task. I never stepped foot in Electrical or Security this entire round. \n\nFrank, you saw me in Medbay at tick 19 because I was finishing that scan after coming down from Cafeteria. You then walked into Electrical and immediately reported. From my perspective, you could easily be self-reporting Eve's body, but I'm not going to hard accuse you just yet because Charlie is completely unaccounted for. \n\nNone of the three of us (Diana, Frank, myself) saw Alice all round either. Charlie, where were you this whole time? You're the only one who might be linked to Alice's death.\n\nListen, everyone: there are 4 of us alive and 2 dead. We are at MYLO (miss-or-lose). If we vote out an innocent Goose right now, the Duck just needs one more kill to win the game. Since I know I'm innocent, if you guess and vote me, we lose. Unless Charlie's route is completely completely fake or someone confesses, we absolutely cannot afford to risk a wrong vote. We should skip, stay grouped next round, and catch the Duck in the act."}}
{"timestamp": 1779379673.722181, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "My route was security \u2192 weapons \u2192 security \u2192 electrical \u2192 medbay \u2192 upper engine \u2192 lower engine.\n\nImportant: I saw Alice alive in Weapons at ticks 3-5. She entered Weapons from Security at tick 3, and I stayed there briefly with her. I did not see a body when I left. I also saw Eve alive in Medbay around tick 12.\n\nSo from my POV: Eve was definitely alive after Diana last saw her leaving upper engine, and she was in the medbay/electrical side later. Bob being in Medbay at tick 19 right before Frank reports Eve in Electrical is really relevant.\n\nAlso, Bob\u2019s route says he went to Weapons after Medbay early. That\u2019s the last place I saw Alice alive. I didn\u2019t see Bob while I was there, so he may have come after I left \u2014 but that puts him near Alice\u2019s last known location too.\n\nFrank and Diana seem to partially confirm each other around lower engine ticks 12-14. I\u2019m not clearing Frank completely because self-report is possible, but Bob\u2019s story connects to both deaths: Weapons for Alice\u2019s last known spot, and Medbay right next to Electrical for Eve\u2019s body. I think Bob is the strongest suspect here."}}
{"timestamp": 1779379694.996928, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I\u2019m still leaning Bob here. My own route is confirmed in parts by Diana, and Charlie\u2019s info puts Bob near both relevant areas: Weapons where Alice was last seen alive, and Medbay right next to Electrical right before I reported Eve.\n\nBob saying \u201cwe should skip\u201d worries me too. With two dead, we need to use the info we have, and Bob has the most opportunity based on everyone\u2019s routes. I don\u2019t think this is a guaranteed lock, but if we\u2019re voting, my vote is Bob."}}
{"timestamp": 1779379722.4260118, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I still think Bob is the strongest suspect from the combined info.\n\nMy confirmed info is: Bob was in Medbay early coming from Electrical, then Eve went from Upper Engine toward Medbay at tick 9, and later Charlie says Eve was alive in Medbay around tick 12. Frank was with/near me in Lower Engine ticks 12-14, so that makes Frank less likely for Eve at least during that window.\n\nThen Frank sees Bob in Medbay at tick 19 right before finding Eve in Electrical. That places Bob closest to Eve\u2019s body. And Charlie\u2019s Weapons info also makes Bob\u2019s claimed route line up with where Alice was last seen.\n\nI agree we shouldn\u2019t random vote at 4, but this isn\u2019t random \u2014 Bob is connected to both death areas, and his \u201cskip, we can\u2019t risk it\u201d argument feels like trying to avoid the vote when the evidence is landing on him. I\u2019m voting Bob unless something major changes."}}
{"timestamp": 1779379738.385746, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Guys, you are making a massive mistake and letting the real Duck manipulate you. Frank and Diana, you are partially clearing each other for ticks 12-14, which is fine, but look at Charlie's timeline. He claims he went Security \u2192 Weapons \u2192 Security \u2192 Electrical \u2192 Medbay \u2192 Upper Engine \u2192 Lower Engine. That is a ridiculously long route, and he is miraculously placing himself as the \"last witness\" at both crime scenes to control the narrative. \n\nAnd Frank, you walked into Electrical and reported Eve. You could easily have killed her right then. If I was the Duck and killed Eve in Electrical, why on earth would I just casually stand in Medbay right next door until tick 19 waiting for you to see me? That makes absolutely zero sense. A Duck would have fled to Storage or Cafeteria. I was doing my Submit Scan.\n\nIf you vote me, an innocent Goose, we drop to 3 players and the Duck just needs one kill to win. The game will be over. Charlie's route is incredibly suspicious and convenient. I'm voting Charlie, and if you want to win, you should look closely at him or Frank's self-report instead of taking the easy bait on me."}}
{"timestamp": 1779379760.0803359, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "Bob, my route is not \u201cridiculously long\u201d \u2014 it\u2019s basically a loop through connected rooms: Security to Weapons, back through Security/Electrical/Medbay, then engines. That is completely doable in 20 ticks.\n\nWhat matters is the overlap:\n\n- I saw Alice alive in Weapons ticks 3-5.\n- You claim you went to Weapons after early Medbay.\n- I saw Eve alive in Medbay around tick 12.\n- Frank sees you in Medbay at tick 19, then immediately finds Eve dead in Electrical.\n- Electrical is directly next to Medbay.\n\nFrank self-report is possible in theory, but Diana confirms Frank away from that side around ticks 12-14, and your claimed route puts you near both Alice\u2019s last known area and Eve\u2019s death area. That\u2019s not me controlling the narrative \u2014 that\u2019s everyone\u2019s info lining up around you.\n\nI agree a wrong vote is dangerous, but skipping with this much evidence also lets the Duck keep killing. I still think Bob is the best vote."}}
